<ServiceLayout title="Carpal Tunnel" description="Chiropractic treatment for carpal tunnel syndrome at Frey Clinic of Chiropractic in Napoleon, OH." schemaType="MedicalCondition">
<p>Carpal tunnel syndrome causes pain, numbness, and tingling in the hand and fingers. While the compression typically occurs at the wrist, the underlying cause may involve the neck and upper spine as well. Chiropractic care addresses both the local and spinal components of this condition.</p>
<hr class="rule rule--accent" style="margin-block:var(--sp-6);" />
<h2>Beyond the wrist</h2>
<p>Many carpal tunnel cases involve what's called a "double crush" — nerve compression at both the wrist and the cervical spine. Treating only the wrist may provide incomplete relief. Our chiropractors evaluate the entire nerve pathway to ensure comprehensive care.</p>
<h2>Conservative treatment</h2>
<p>Chiropractic care for carpal tunnel may include adjustments to the wrist, elbow, and cervical spine, along with guidance on ergonomics and exercises. Many patients find significant relief without surgery.</p>
</ServiceLayout>
